{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>הכפורים</b> Two times in the Masorah: this one and the other: מדם חטאת הכפורים אחת בשנה יכפר. And this too is a hint to the verse about charity on Yom HaKippurim." "<b>והיה לבנ\"י</b> לזכרן — plene, with vav. לזכרון — defective, without vav, for they were not לזכרון except while still on his shoulders, but once they were established and standing they were no longer לזכרון:" "<b>(ח) ועשית כיור</b> The kiyyor is juxtaposed to the passage of shekels to teach that rains are withheld on account of those who pledge charity and do not give. <b>לרחצה</b> — four times in the Masorah: every kiyyor that does not hold enough for four priests to wash from it simultaneously is not a kiyyor:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The juxtaposition of the two occurrences of הכפרים/הכפורים is read as linking the atonement-money of our verse to the Yom Kippur atonement of the second occurrence; the final clause hints that the half-shekel charity effects atonement like Yom Kippur.", 1 "The notarikon בנ\"י expands לבני ישראל; the comment contrasts the plene spelling of לזכרן with the defective spelling of לזכרון, referring to the stones on the High Priest's shoulders (Exodus 28:12).", 2 "The verse number (ח) = 8 refers to the chapter or verse numbering in the original; the four occurrences of לרחצה are cited without addresses as is standard in his Masorah comments."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:51.544721138Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}